      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:6:2:59:4",
      "text": [
        " قُلْتُ لِأَبِي عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) رَجُلٌ قَالَ لِامْرَأَتِهِ أَنْتِ عَلَيَّ حَرَامٌ قَالَ لَيْسَ عَلَيْهِ كَفَّارَةٌ وَ لَا طَلَاقٌ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Humeyd, from Ibn Sama’at, from Safwan, from Hareyz, from Muhammad Bin Muslim who said, ",
          "‘I said to Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup>, ‘A man says to his wife, ‘You are prohibited unto me’’. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘There is no expiation upon him, nor a divorce’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "4. Humayd ibn Ziyad has narrated from ibn Sama‘ah from Safwan from Hariz from Muhammad ibn Muslim who has said the following: “I once asked abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about the case of a man who says to his wife, ‘You are unlawful for me.’ He (the Imam) said, ‘There is no expiation on him and it is not a divorce.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
